ID: vr-06
Title: Qualify a free-local CPU speech-to-face inference path
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/5

Status: DONE
Milestone: Actual bounded CPU inference evidence before backend adoption.
Dependencies: vr-05

Purpose:
Honor the owner's choice to keep everything free and local on the current AMD
machine. Investigate standard ONNX execution of the publicly released A2F Mark
regression network before accepting the larger UniTalker dependency/asset path.
This is a custom CPU experiment, not official SDK CPU support.

Tasks:
[x] Record the owner's free/local-only compute decision.
[x] Inspect exact model assets, license and inference/reconstruction contracts.
[x] Isolate CPU dependencies and bound threads/work size on the shared machine.
[x] Run a small numerical inference/reconstruction check, reporting real failures.
[x] Record measured feasibility separately from articulation/human acceptance.
[x] Reconcile documentation, issue/Project tracking and private continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
No CUDA, paid service, remote inference, recording upload or device activation.
Model/runtime versions and asset hashes are explicit; no untrusted pickle load.
Finite, correctly shaped outputs are necessary but not a claim of accurate speech.
If the model cannot run here, report the exact blocker rather than faking motion.
No changes to global packages, sibling runtimes or other users' processes.

Completion evidence:
Chapter 05 documents pinned assets, exact data/conditioning/PCA contracts,
reproduction commands, measured results and explicit omissions.
CPU-only ORT1.23.2 produced finite [30,301] output and [61520,3] skin geometry.
One synthetic non-speech second: median network20.26ms/frame, total0.613s;
single skin reconstruction6.56ms. Not end-to-end speed or speech accuracy.
Nine focused checks and dependency consistency passed. No persistent process.
Stable issue5 and unique Project item verified using saved identities; owned
continuity records the free/local choice, actual CPU result and remaining gates.
Seven book sources and local links/required workstream fields checked.

Completion log:
2026-11-18 - Owner selected "Keep everything free and local on this AMD machine".
Public metadata suggests a custom ONNX CPU experiment; not yet a working backend.
2026-11-18 - Actual CPU inference and PCA succeeded using pinned public assets,
isolated NumPy/ORT, two inference threads and no CUDA or remote inference.
Synthetic input only. Full SDK postprocess, topology/player and real-speech
qualification remain future work; do not call the whole app complete.
2026-11-18 - Source/book, focused validation, local-only model/env receipts,
issue/backlink/Project identity and continuity reconciled. This finite numerical
feasibility task is complete; full speaking-face implementation remains open.
